//------------------------------- Teleport -------------------------------//

@99991 = ~Weird Ring~
@99992 = ~Wonder~
@99993 = ~For some reason, whenever your casual gaze rests upon this unremarkable ring, its smooth surface seems to shimmer with shifting hues, yet upon careful scrutiny nothing particularly distinctive is revealed.~
@99994 = ~Ring of Torto: Wonder

At the edge of the marshes where Tethyr meets Amn, upon the rotting wooden dock outside Watcher's Keep, this plain, unadorned ring has been picked up more than once, and more than once has it lost its bearer.

The most reliable account of it survives in the ledger of an Athkatlan antiquities dealer. Some forty years ago, a merchant named Wulven bought it in Waukeen's Promenade for three silver pieces, taking it for little more than a botched piece of darkened copper discarded by an apprentice. That changed one night as he sat beneath his lamp, taking stock of a shipment purportedly unearthed from Netherese ruins. Out of the corner of his eye, he caught an oily iridescence rippling across the copper band on his finger. He looked down to examine it, only to find the ring pitch-dark and quite unremarkable; yet when he raised his eyes back to the crate, every illusory glamour within fell away at once. A gilded staff stood revealed as bare pine, and an amulet etched with intricate runes reverted to a common pebble. Only a forgotten, rusted iron nail in the corner met his gaze differently. Without warning, its buried past laid itself open before him: he knew at once that it had pinned the keel of a warship sunk off the Sword Coast, and found the long-dead shipwright's very name rising unbidden to his lips.

With the ring's aid, Wulven exposed half the guild's frauds, yet the more he came to rely on it, the deeper his unease grew regarding its origins. Eventually, he pulled discreet strings and spent half his life's savings to retain a reclusive diviner. Yet an ordinary Identify spell yielded scarcely more than a single word: "Wonder". When the mage turned instead to the costly casting of Legend Lore, the magic struck the ring as though hitting a silent wall; no record of its forging lingered in the Weave, nor was there a trace of it in the annals of the gods. Before the spell unraveled, it salvaged only a fragmented name from the rifts of time: "Torto".

No chronicle in Candlekeep had ever recorded that name, yet Wulven hunted for word of it as though possessed. Over time, he noticed that whenever he approached ancient ruins where the fabric of space had worn thin, the ring would once more take on that faint, uncanny sheen no eye could squarely meet. Years later, deep into autumn, the old man sold off everything he owned and followed the old road into the wilds of Tethyr. The last soul to see him was a passing peddler: Wulven stood alone at the end of the wooden dock before Watcher's Keep, gazing down at that strange, unconcealed hue upon his finger. Once a bank of thick mist drifted past and cleared, the dock was empty. Nothing remained save this ordinary-looking ring, lying quietly between the damp planks, waiting for the next passerby to inadvertently catch it shifting color.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
Lore: +100

Special abilities:
Teleport
True Seeing three times per day~

@99995 = ~The Teleport ability has been anchored, only active on the Watcher's Keep entrance map.~

